---
// The problem — section 2 of the home-page skeleton (mt#3827).
// Plain language throughout; no undefined register vocabulary.
---

<section id="problem" class="content-section" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
  <div class="content-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
    <h2 id="problem-heading" class="section-headline">The bottleneck is you.</h2>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>
        An agent handles a single, well-scoped task well — write this function, fix this bug,
        add this test. Sustained work is different: dozens of tasks in flight, changes that need
        review, mistakes that need remembering, decisions that need a person. Point an agent at
        real, ongoing work and the well-scoped-task skill stops covering it.
      </p>
      <p>
        What fills the gap is you. You track what each agent is doing, because nothing else
        does. You review every change, because nothing else will catch a bad one. You clean up
        abandoned branches and half-finished sessions, because nothing else notices they stalled.
        You are the dispatcher, the reviewer, and the janitor — all at once, for every agent you
        run.
      </p>
      <p>That works for one agent. It does not scale to two, and it collapses well before ten.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .content-section {
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-text-primary) 4%, transparent);
  }
  .content-inner {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .section-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .section-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.125rem;
  }
  .section-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
</style>
